## 1. Process narrative

Three vertical turbine raw-water pumps (P-101 / P-102 / P-103, 3.0 MGD each)
lift Cedar River water from the intake wet well through the 24" raw main to the
Cedar Ridge WTP. A motorized slide gate (GATE) throttles river inflow to the
wet well. Lead/lag duty automatically rotates among pumps placed in AUTO.

Pumps run in one of three modes per pump (HR 0/1/2): `0 = OFF`, `1 = HAND`,
`2 = AUTO`. In AUTO the station starts the lead pump on rising wet-well level
and the lag pump at a higher level; both stop on falling level. In HAND the
operator starts/stops the pump directly with its HAND_RUN coil.

