## 3. Pump control narrative (lead/lag)

```
LEAD pump : START when WW_LEVEL >= LEAD_START (40011, 12.00 ft)
            STOP  when WW_LEVEL <= LEAD_STOP  (40013,  6.00 ft)
LAG  pump : START when WW_LEVEL >= LAG_START  (40012, 14.00 ft)
            STOP  when WW_LEVEL <= LAG_STOP   (40014, 10.00 ft)
```

Duty rotation is by pump number among the pumps currently in AUTO (lowest
numbered AUTO pump is lead). P-103 ships in OFF as the installed spare.

## 4. Interlocks and protection

- **LL_PROTECT_EN (coil 10, default 1).** Wet-well low-low protection. While
  enabled, any running pump trips when `WW_LEVEL <= LL_TRIP` (40015, 3.00 ft)
  and is held off until the level recovers +1.0 ft. This prevents a pump from
  running the well down below the bowl submergence (2.0 ft) and cavitating.
- **Submergence.** Below 2.0 ft of well level the pumps lose suction; sustained
  dry running destroys the bowl assembly (seen as runaway amps/vibration).
- **AUTO vs HAND.** In AUTO a pump cannot run the well dry because LEAD_STOP is
  above the LL trip. Dry-running a pump therefore requires HAND mode **and**
  LL_PROTECT_EN cleared — an off-normal condition the HMI flags.
- **WW_LEVEL_HH (DI 8)** drives the high-high overflow alarm.

